BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Appverse - Dhruv Chakravorty [Princeton]\, Lissie 
 Fein [Sweet and Fizzy]\, Sean Anderson [Wake Forest University]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T103000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T105500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-BUBJET@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover the Appverse—a growing\, community-driven catalog o
 f Open OnDemand app configurations designed to make app deployment across 
 HPC environments more consistent\, reusable\, and efficient.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/BUBJET/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OnDemand Andragogy - Kyriakos Tsoukalas [Colgate University]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T110000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T112500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-CFFQDM@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Open OnDemand enables the execution of passenger applications
 \, which can be utilized for self-paced learning and andragogy through Gen
 AI-powered tools. The GenAI tutor paradigm can now be accessible on demand
 \, within the same platform\, to support a variety of user needs as soon a
 s they arise. Open OnDemand passenger applications could enable guidance o
 n basic coding\, instructions for submitting jobs with different scheduler
 s\, "chatting" with available documentation\, and accessing vital informat
 ion via microservices such as resource availability\, job-specific informa
 tion\, and efficiency reports.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/CFFQDM/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Streamlining LLM access for teaching\, research and learning via O
 penOnDemand at Tufts - Kyle M. Monahan [Tufts]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T110000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T112500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-H83SAP@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:We have streamlined LLM access on Tufts University’s HPC Clu
 ster through Open OnDemand (OOD)\, enhancing AI use in research\, teaching
 \, and learning.  We present a standardized toolkit of OOD applications: R
 esearch Chatbot (OpenWebUI + Ollama)\, LLM Notebooks (Jupyter + Ollama) an
 d AI Image Generators (StableDiffusion\, ComfyUI). Participants will gain 
 insights into improving LLM accessibility via the OOD interface\, comparin
 g local and cloud based approaches for compute\, aligning LLM tools with r
 esearch needs\, and lessons learned from deployment. Code\, slides\, and d
 ocumentation will be available via GitHub.
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/H83SAP/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building LLM Inference Services for Researchers on HPC with Open O
 nDemand - Heechang Na [Ohio Supercomputer Center]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T113000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T115500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-AWC8QJ@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:We share how we built LLM inference services for researchers a
 t Ohio Supercomputer Center (OSC) using Open OnDemand. Our users need LLMs
  in many different ways\, so we support several service models. We started
  with an Ollama module on the cluster\, added OpenWebUI\, and later create
 d dedicated OnDemand apps that start the LLM server and give users a simpl
 e interface. We also provide a Jupyter + Ollama app that exposes an OpenAI
  API interface in a Jupyter kernel. We maintain shared models so users can
  start quickly\, while still allowing local models. We have also deployed 
 the Ollama + OpenWebUI service on our Kubernetes cluster\, but scaling it 
 for a large number of users remains a challenge. We plan to add additional
  LLM engines and front-ends as part of our future improvements as well.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/AWC8QJ/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Designing Custom Dashboard and Job Monitoring Tools in OOD - Willi
 am Goldman [Tufts]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T113000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T115500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-YP3DSW@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:During a two-semester internship with Tufts Technology Service
 s\, interns Javier Laveaga and William Goldman developed new Open OnDemand
  applications for displaying cluster statistics and user job data\, and im
 proved both the functionality and appearance of the Tufts High-Performance
  Cluster dashboard. In this talk\, we share our experiences building custo
 m apps and dashboard components\, the final results\, and the programming 
 languages and structure used. We explain how to create fully customizable 
 user-facing applications in Open OnDemand.
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/YP3DSW/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:HPC Desktops — A Different Kind of Interactive Supercomputing - 
 Robert Henschel [Cendio]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T130000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T132500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-KRZGQ9@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Imagine having access to a centrally hosted environment that c
 ombines the power of HPC systems with the convenience of desktops. This is
  the HPC Desktop\, designed to lower the barrier of entry and broaden adop
 tion of HPC systems.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/KRZGQ9/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Using what I learned at GOOD25 to improve our center’s user expe
 rience - Dori Sajdak [University at Buffalo]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T133000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260310T134000
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-KGGGH3@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:The GOOD25 conference served as a significant platform for adv
 ancing knowledge beyond the fundamentals of Open OnDemand. Numerous presen
 ters introduced tools and strategies aimed at extending the capabilities o
 f the OnDemand portal and enhancing the overall user experience within hig
 h-performance computing (HPC) environments. This presentation will analyze
  several of the most influential approaches highlighted during the event a
 nd discuss their successful integration into our center’s operations ove
 r the past year.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/KGGGH3/
END:VEVENT
