BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open OnDemand Project Update - Julie Ma [Massachusetts Green High 
 Performance Computing Center]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T090000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T092500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-PAHRWR@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:A core leadership update on recent Open OnDemand updates\, new
  cross-cutting solutions\, update on teh OOD affinity Groups\, and more.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/PAHRWR/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workflow Management in Open OnDemand - Harshit Soora [University o
 f Maryland]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T093000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T095500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-ZEZHQX@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Executing multi-task computational research workflows on HPC s
 ystems often requires manual scripting\, resource manager and scheduler ex
 pertise. It creates barriers for researchers and educators\, especially at
  smaller institutions or in multidisciplinary collaborations. Although OOD
  provides an accessible web-based interface for launching standalone appli
 cations as jobs\, it has lacked an integrated mechanism to easily compose
 \, manage\, and execute multiple tasks with dependencies among them as Wor
 kflows. Workflows enabled researchers to visually construct\, execute\, an
 d monitor simple composition of multiple “launchers” (i.e. independent
  tasks/jobs) that can perform data pre- or post-processing\, simulation\, 
 and other computational tasks connected via output to input dependencies.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/ZEZHQX/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MATLAB + OOD: Parallel Computing and GenAI with MATLAB Copilot - N
 ick Choi [MathWorks]\, Lisa Kempler [MathWorks]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T100000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T102500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-FDKCP9@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Since GOOD 2025\, more HPC Centers have been adopting Open OnD
 emand. Many sites have integrated MATLAB. Learn what’s new and which too
 ls sites are offering\, including:\n-	Browser-based access to full MATLAB
 \, including GPU and parallel computing tools \n-	MATLAB Copilot for GenAI
 -assisted coding and simulation in cloud and desktop  \n-	MATLAB MCP Core 
 Server for integrating MATLAB with agentic AIs
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/FDKCP9/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Modular Dashboard Framework for Customizable & Accessible High P
 erformance Computing - Sahil Vartak [Texas A&M University]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T100000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T102500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-A3FWHS@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:As HPC expands beyond computer science\, many users encounter 
 command-line interfaces for the first time. HPCMosaic addresses this gap w
 ith a modular OOD dashboard that simplifies cluster management for non-tec
 hnical researchers while staying customizable for experienced users. This 
 talk presents a framework that reduces support burden by enabling self-ser
 vice for common tasks (file quotas\, account management\, and job control)
  decreasing repetitive tickets. Targeted at HPC developers and cluster adm
 ins\, this session covers modern dashboard development focused on customiz
 ability and user experience. Attendees will learn how to build accessible 
 HPC interfaces that let researchers focus on their work instead of trouble
 shooting\, reducing user frustration and support workload.
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/A3FWHS/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Simplifying Cloud Computing: Integration of Open OnDemand with O
 penStack - Andrej Čermák [CESNET]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T110000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T112500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-ATV33X@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:At CESNET we have integrated OpenStack with Open OnDemand\, 
 enabling users to create and deploy virtual machines\, Kubernetes clusters
  and applications with minimal effort. In this presentation we will demons
 trate the full potential of this integration through two concrete use‑ca
 ses: (1) provisioning a simple OpenStack virtual machine and (2) launching
  an on‑premises Kubernetes deployment. The talk will highlight the under
 lying adapter architecture\, share technical insights from the implementat
 ion\, and discuss current limitations and challenges. The goal is to provi
 de an overview for any organization that provides OpenStack to its users a
 nd wishes to support this functionality.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/ATV33X/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Domain-Aware Workflow Monitoring in Open OnDemand - Owen Schillaci
  [Texas A&M University]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T110000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T112500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-DSFY7V@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Researchers rely on Open OnDemand (OOD) to design\, launch\, a
 nd manage scientific workflows on high performance computing (HPC) systems
 . In addition to job creation and submission\, this process also includes 
 monitoring job progress. OOD provides the job-listing app and session card
 s for monitoring running jobs. However\, these tools primarily provide sch
 eduler-level information\, forcing researchers to manually retrieve workfl
 ow and domain-specific information. Drona Workflow Engine bridges this gap
  by providing integrated\, domain-specific monitoring throughout the workf
 low lifecycle. In this presentation\, we will focus on job-monitoring capa
 bilities and explore various types of job monitoring integrated into the r
 epresentative\, commonly used scientific workflows.
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/DSFY7V/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Zero to Productive: Open OnDemand on Azure CycleCloud for Slu
 rm-with Entra ID\,VS Code\,AI Agents - Xavier Pillons [Microsoft]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T113000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T115500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-QXWWZH@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Open OnDemand (OOD) provides researchers with a streamlined\, 
 browser-based HPC experience. This session covers deploying and operating 
 OOD on Azure CycleCloud Workspace for Slurm\, including provisioning the O
 OD VM\, integrating Microsoft Entra ID with OpenID Connect and federated c
 redentials\, and auto-registering Slurm clusters for dynamic partition dis
 covery. We'll demo browser-based VS Code for interactive development\, exp
 lore when to use Cendio ThinLinc for enhanced visualization\, and show how
  AI Agents like GitHub Copilot inside VS Code can rapidly build new OOD ap
 ps and templates.
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/QXWWZH/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Implementing and Configuring User Impersonation - Brandon Biggs [I
 daho National Lab]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T113000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T115500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-CCJPZN@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:User impersonation is a powerful capability within Open OnDema
 nd that enables designated users—such as administrators\, support staff
 \, or service accounts—to act on behalf of other users to troubleshoot i
 ssues\, validate configurations\, and streamline workflows. As HPC centers
  grow more complex and support demands increase\, a flexible and secure im
 personation model becomes essential.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/CCJPZN/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Job Sharing Between Users with Multitenant Apps - Sean Anderson [W
 ake Forest University]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T130000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T132500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-YJEYT9@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:The Multitenant Apps framework was developed for supporting LL
 Ms\, databases\, and other services on traditional\, job-based HPC infrast
 ructure through Open OnDemand (OOD). It allows for controlled and secure s
 haring of these services between select users\, and can greatly reduce har
 dware overhead since users share the same resources. It is also an effecti
 ve method for delivering content to users within the OOD interface\, which
  is especially useful within classrooms\, research groups\, and even depar
 tments. Featuring an interactive demo!
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/YJEYT9/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Repurposed Hardware to Modern Research: Deploying projectEUREKA! O
 pen OnDemand and Kubernetes - Boyd Wilson [Omnibond]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T130000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T132500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-CH7TWT@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:As AI\, HPC\, and data-intensive research workloads continue t
 o grow\, many institutions face a common challenge: how to modernize resea
 rch computing environments without replacing existing infrastructure\, exp
 anding staff\, or locking into proprietary platforms. This talk presents a
  real-world case study of deploying projectEUREKA! with integrated Open On
 Demand\, an AI and HPC orchestration platform on Kubernetes\, using a repu
 rposed on-premises HPC cluster at Texas A&M University–San Antonio (TAMU
 SA).\nWe describe how Kubernetes was used as a local orchestration layer\,
  enabling flexible\, project-centric workflows across resources\, while pr
 oviding a browser-based experience. Demonstrates how institutions can exte
 nd the life of existing hardware\, simplify user access\, and support mode
 rn workflows.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/CH7TWT/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bridging AI and Biomedical Workflows via Containerized Apps in Ope
 n OnDemand - Shane Corder [Moffitt Cancer Center]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T133000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T135500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-UKAQCF@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:HPC faces a dual challenge of supporting AI/ML engineers along
 side domain-specific researchers who may lack Linux expertise. This presen
 tation explores leveraging OOD as a unified gateway for cancer research an
 d AI/ML pipelines. We detail our technical strategy of configuring OOD int
 eractive applications to launch and manage Apptainer containers. This stra
 tegy delivers portable\, reproducible\, and version-controlled software st
 acks - from GPU-accelerated PyTorch environments to GUI-based biomedical v
 isualization tools\, effectively democratizing access to HPC by abstractin
 g the complexity of the container runtime and Slurm. We share how this app
 roach provides a low entry barrier for oncologists/biologists\, environmen
 tal consistency for AI experts\, and reduces support burden.
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/UKAQCF/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open OnDemand in the EuroHPC Federation Platform - Robin Karlsson 
 [CSC - IT Center for Science]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T133000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T135500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-CZBTDH@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:The EuroHPC Federation Platform is a project to federate acces
 s to EuroHPC systems\, to make it\neasier for researchers and industry use
 rs across Europe to access computing resources. Within\nthe project\, a fe
 derated instance of Open OnDemand has been developed and deployed. It has 
 many\nunique features and integrations\, such as remote cluster file syste
 m access\, Kubernetes-native\ndeployment\, and integration of the EESSI so
 ftware stack.\nThis talk targets system administrators\, service owners\, 
 and others interested in federation of HPC\nresources or responsible for m
 aintaining and developing Open OnDemand instances. It discusses\ntechnical
  details and challenges of providing a single instance of Open OnDemand wh
 ich is\nconnected to multiple supercomputers at external organizations.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/CZBTDH/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:KROOD: Kubernetes Running Open OnDemand - Aaron Janssen [North Dak
 ota State University]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T140000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T142500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-SFDZPQ@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Kubernetes has emerged as a *de facto* standard for deploying 
 distributed systems and complex\, multi-service web applications\, and is 
 gaining popularity in HPC environments. Given its demonstrated utility for
  research computing\, how can we leverage Kubernetes for orchestrating  Op
 en OnDemand (OOD) deployments? In this talk\, we present a Kubernetes oper
 ator we developed for deploying and managing OOD inside a Kubernetes clust
 er. We demonstrate how our operator can be used with a pilot implementatio
 n of a Kubernetes-native OOD architecture that allows for network availabl
 e PUNs and advanced scheduling. Finally\, we’ll close with a discussion 
 of the pros\, cons\, and potential use cases for the KROOD approach to OOD
  management.
LOCATION:Breakout Room
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/SFDZPQ/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Simplified Approach to Managing Your Data with Globus - Greg Naw
 rocki [Globus]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T140000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T142500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-SSXDD9@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Open OnDemand and Globus are natural partners: Open OnDemand l
 owers the barrier to using advanced computing resources while Globus adds 
 managed services to simplify data transfer\, distributed computation and w
 orkflow automation. Using Globus to move and share data\, provide high per
 formance remote function execution and at-scale automation\, makes your Op
 en OnDemand system even more valuable to researchers. In this talk we will
  demonstrate how the two systems integrate to help researchers curate data
  from inception to publication.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/SSXDD9/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open OnDemand Developer Team Open Mic - Emily Moffat Sadeghi [Ohio
  Supercomputer Center]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T150000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T152500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-BLMTQM@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Meet with Open OnDemand Dev team members to ask questions abou
 t the platform and the docs that don’t easily lend themselves to discour
 se or email. Community members are welcome to chime in on topics outside t
 he scope of what is deployed at Ohio Supercomputer Center.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/BLMTQM/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Supporting Interactive Graphical Applications with ThinLinc in Ope
 n OnDemand - Robert Henschel [Cendio]\, Mattias Reuterskiöld [Cendio]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T153000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T155500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-TDP7YW@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:This session will introduce ThinLinc and how to use it togethe
 r with Open OnDemand. ThinLinc is a Linux terminal server solution that is
  used at HPC centers around the world to support access to interactive gra
 phical Linux applications. The ThinLinc team is working with the OOD team 
 to integrate ThinLinc into OOD and this session will go over the technical
  work as well as the features of the integration. This session will also i
 nclude a demo of the current beta release.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/TDP7YW/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Wizard for Complexity: Inspiring New UI/UX for HPC Applications 
 - Sahil Vartak [Texas A&M University]\, Owen Schillaci [Texas A&M Universi
 ty]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T163000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T164000
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-DEVBWX@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:LAMMPS's complex\, non-uniform GPU feature support creates a d
 ilemma: users struggle to find a compatible build\, leading to wasted time
 \, admin overload\, and underutilized GPUs (e.g.\, Intel Max). We present 
 an intelligent\, wizard-style utility that performs **automatic three-way 
 matchmaking** between available LAMMPS software builds\, GPU accelerators
 \, and user input requirements. The utility suggests optimal\, GPU-acceler
 ated builds and clearly explains why others are incompatible. Built atop t
 he Drona job launcher\, the wizard uses dynamically repopulating menus to 
 guide users through the selection process\, and finally injects the full c
 onfiguration directly into a ready-to-run Slurm job script.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/DEVBWX/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Accessible LLM Inference via Open OnDemand - Keegan [Texas A&M Uni
 versity]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T164000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T165000
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-DDCDPV@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Large language models are now a common tool for writing code a
 nd exploring ideas\, but using them on HPC systems can still be a challeng
 e. To make this simpler\, I built an interactive Open OnDemand application
  that lets users access a local LLM directly inside Jupyter Notebook using
  the Jupyter AI extension. Behind the scenes\, user requests are routed th
 rough a load balancer to a pool of vLLM inference servers running on Intel
  GPUs\, which serve open-source models up to 70B parameters.\n\nIn this ta
 lk\, I’ll walk through how the system works\, why we built it\, and how 
 it gives researchers easy\, reliable access to LLM assistance without rely
 ing on external cloud services.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/DDCDPV/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Auto Machine Learning on Open OnDemand - Keegan [Texas A&M Univers
 ity]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T165000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T170000
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-XNUVDC@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:Machine learning now plays a very important role in a wide ran
 ge of scientific fields. However many researchers in these scientific fiel
 ds don't have machine learning expertise and may find it difficult to trai
 n a machine learning model themselves. \nAuto machine learning bridges thi
 s gap by making it very simple to train a state of the art model. Auto mac
 hine learning frameworks like AutoGluon make it such that all you need is 
 a dataset and a few lines of code.  \nThe interactive application that I h
 ave developed for Open OnDemand closes the gap further by not requiring th
 e user to write any code at all. Through our application\, users can simpl
 y choose a dataset and their configuration\, and train the model.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/XNUVDC/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OnDemand Application Development Internship at Tufts - Delilah Mal
 oney [Tufts]\, Yucheng Zhang [Tufts]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T170000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T171000
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-87KRTL@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:We are excited to share insights from the inaugural OnDemand i
 nternship hosted by Research Technology at Tufts Technology Services. This
  presentation highlights the interns’ accomplishments\, explores challen
 ges encountered\, and identifies opportunities uncovered. We look forward 
 to sharing our journey and lessons learned with fellow HPC centers.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/87KRTL/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CryoSPARC Interactive App Deployment - Michael Dickens [Texas A&M 
 University]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T171000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T172000
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-KYBWAV@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:CryoSPARC is a leading cryo‑EM data‑processing platform. W
 hile CryoSPARC offers various installation methods\, each can pose signifi
 cant challenges for HPC users and system administrators ranging from versi
 on updates to port management.\n\nTo streamline deployment\, we have creat
 ed a CryoSPARC interactive app and a script for generating a Singularity i
 mage that eliminates the need for end‑users to perform any manual instal
 lation. This OOD app utilizes a CryoSPARC Singularity image that is shared
  among all users while providing each user with their own individual datab
 ase and log files. This dramatically reduces storage overhead and simplifi
 es version control\, while providing each researcher with a fully function
 al CryoSPARC environment.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/KYBWAV/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Intuitive\, Extensible Open OnDemand Dashboard for Job Accounti
 ng and Performance Metrics - Richie Tan [Purdue]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T172000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260311T173000
DTSTAMP:20261020T211525Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-PKB37G@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:High-performance computing allows researchers across the globe
  to conduct research at scale. At Purdue University\, Open OnDemand provid
 es an easy way for users to access cluster resources and launch popular ap
 plications with minimal barriers. In order to improve how users interact w
 ith clusters\, we are building a user-friendly\, modular web dashboard on 
 Open OnDemand with detailed\, organized cluster information and color-code
 d visualizations. By combining Slurm-based data sources and modular widget
 s and components\, this dashboard allows researchers to access cluster inf
 ormation about their jobs and allocations easily and provides a modular\, 
 extensible framework to install on any Slurm-based cluster.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/PKB37G/
END:VEVENT
